I now have a complete picture. Here is the thorough report.

## Overview

This is an OfficeFloor + Spring PetClinic hybrid. `POST /api/owners` is defined by a YAML "composition" that chains Java function classes into a pipeline. The request/response DTOs are NOT hand-written source files — they are generated at build time from `openapi.yml` (via the openapi-generator-maven-plugin) into `target/generated-sources/openapi/.../rest/dto/` (package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`). So to change DTO fields/validation you edit `openapi.yml`.

---

## 1. Owner YAML files (create pipeline and related)

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`
```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

validate:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.ValidateOwnerFields
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: build

build:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.BuildOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: save

save:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.SaveOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond

respond:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RespondWithOwnerCreated
  govern: [ transaction ]
```
Create pipeline: `ValidateOwnerFields -> BuildOwner -> SaveOwner -> RespondWithOwnerCreated`.

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` (update, for contrast)
```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

validate:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.ValidateOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: load
load:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.LoadOwner
  next: apply
apply:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.ApplyOwner
  next: save
save:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.SaveOwner
  next: respond
respond:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RespondWithOwnerUpdated
```
(Other owner YAMLs: `owners.GET.yml`, `owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml`, `owners/{ownerId}.DELETE.yml`, `v2/owners.GET.yml`, plus nested pet endpoints under `owners/{ownerId}/pets...`.)

---

## 2. Java function classes in the create pipeline

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerFields.java`
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner;

import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;
import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Out;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.OwnerFieldsDto;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestBody;

/**
 * Rejects a create request that is missing or blank in any required field
 * (firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone) before {@link BuildOwner} maps the
 * body, reporting every offending field at once...
 */
public class ValidateOwnerFields {

    public void service(@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated)
            throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
        List<String> missing = new ArrayList<>();
        requireText(missing, "firstName", request.getFirstName());
        requireText(missing, "lastName", request.getLastName());
        requireText(missing, "address", request.getAddress());
        requireText(missing, "city", request.getCity());
        requireText(missing, "telephone", request.getTelephone());
        if (!missing.isEmpty()) {
            throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missing);
        }
        validated.set(request);
    }

    private static void requireText(List<String> missing, String field, String value) {
        if (value == null || value.isBlank()) {
            missing.add(field);
        }
    }
}
```
This is the only place the request body is bound in the create pipeline (it publishes the validated `OwnerFieldsDto` via `Out`). This is the natural spot to add telephone normalization/format rules before build.

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner;

import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Out;
import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Val;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.mapper.OwnerMapper;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.Owner;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.OwnerFieldsDto;

public class BuildOwner {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
        built.set(ownerMapper.toOwner(request));
    }
}
```

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/SaveOwner.java`
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner;

import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Val;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.Owner;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.repository.OwnerRepository;

public class SaveOwner {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        ownerRepository.save(owner);
    }
}
```

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner;

import java.net.URI;
import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Val;
import net.officefloor.web.ObjectResponse;
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.mapper.OwnerMapper;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.Owner;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.OwnerDto;

public class RespondWithOwnerCreated {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper,
            ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<OwnerDto>> response) {
        OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
        response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/owners/" + owner.getId())).body(dto));
    }
}
```

### Related PUT-pipeline classes (share `SaveOwner`)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwner.java` — binds `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (triggers bean validation -> `MethodArgumentNotValidException` on constraint violations):
```java
@Validated
public class ValidateOwner {
    public void service(@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated) {
        validated.set(request);
    }
}
```
`ApplyOwner.java` copies fields (incl. `setTelephone`) onto a loaded Owner; `LoadOwner.java` looks up by id.

Note: the create pipeline uses `ValidateOwnerFields` (manual not-blank check, no `@Valid`), whereas the update pipeline uses `ValidateOwner` (`@Valid`). The OpenAPI-declared bean-validation constraints on telephone are therefore only enforced on PUT unless you add `@Valid`/normalization to the create path.

---

## 3. Owner entity + DTOs (telephone + validation)

### DTOs are GENERATED (no editable source files)
`OwnerFieldsDto` and `OwnerDto` do not exist as `.java` source files. They are generated from `openapi.yml` by the openapi-generator-maven-plugin (`pom.xml` lines ~369-449): `modelNameSuffix = Dto`, `modelPackage = org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`, output `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java`. Bean-validation annotations on the DTO come from the OpenAPI schema constraints.

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` — `OwnerFields` schema (lines 1991-2039), the source of the telephone field/validation
```yaml
    OwnerFields:
      title: Owner fields
      description: Editable fields of a pet owner.
      type: object
      properties:
        firstName:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 30
          pattern: "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$"
          example: George
        lastName:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 30
          pattern: "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$"
          example: Franklin
        address:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 255
        city:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 80
        telephone:
          title: Telephone number
          description: The telephone number of the pet owner.
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 20
          pattern: '^[0-9]*$'
          example: '6085551023'
      required:
        - firstName
        - lastName
        - address
        - city
        - telephone
```
`Owner` schema (lines 2040+) is `allOf` [`OwnerFields`, {id readOnly int32, pets array}]. The `POST /owners` operation (`addOwner`, lines 65-97) takes `OwnerFields` as request body, returns `Owner` (201), with 400 -> `ProblemDetail`.

Important: the OpenAPI telephone constraint is `maxLength: 20`, `pattern: ^[0-9]*$` (digits only, any length). The acceptance test expects normalization to strip non-digits and require exactly 10 digits — which the current schema does NOT enforce (it allows non-10-digit all-digit strings and rejects the `(04) 1234-5678` input that contains non-digits). This is the gap the tests target.

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — JPA entity (telephone validation)
```java
@Entity
@Table(name = "owners")
public class Owner extends Person {
    @Column(name = "address") @NotEmpty
    private String address;
    @Column(name = "city") @NotEmpty
    private String city;

    @Column(name = "telephone")
    @NotEmpty
    @Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10)
    @Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")
    private String telephone;

    @OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL, mappedBy = "owner", fetch = FetchType.EAGER)
    private Set<Pet> pets;
    // getters/setters incl. getTelephone()/setTelephone(); firstName/lastName inherited from Person
}
```
The entity already enforces exactly-10-digits via `@Pattern("^[0-9]{10}$")` and `@Digits(integer=10)` — but nothing in the create pipeline triggers entity bean-validation, and no normalization strips separators before this. `firstName`/`lastName` live on the `Person` superclass (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java`).

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`
MapStruct mapper. `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` ignores `id` and `pets`; `toOwnerDto(Owner)`; plus collection/page mappers. Field names map straight through (telephone -> telephone).

---

## 4. Owner validation classes

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerFields.java` (create — manual required-field check; full contents above)
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwner.java` (update — `@Valid` bean validation; full contents above)
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/MissingOwnerFieldsException.java`:
```java
public class MissingOwnerFieldsException extends Exception {
    private final List<String> fields;
    public MissingOwnerFieldsException(List<String> fields) {
        super("Missing or blank required owner fields: " + String.join(", ", fields));
        this.fields = List.copyOf(fields);
    }
    public List<String> getFields() { return fields; }
}
```
- `BuildOwner.java` (maps DTO->entity, above).

---

## 5. Tests for owner creation + telephone

There is no unit test per function class; testing is black-box acceptance via MockMvc.

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.acceptance;

import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.springframework.test.web.servlet.result.MockMvcResultMatchers.jsonPath;
import static org.springframework.test.web.servlet.result.MockMvcResultMatchers.status;
import tools.jackson.databind.node.ObjectNode;

/** telephone-normalize: On create, normalize the telephone by removing every non-digit character, then require exa... */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

    @Test
    void coreStripsToTenDigits() throws Exception {
        ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
        o.put("telephone", "(04) 1234-5678");
        int id = createOwnerOk(o);
        getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.telephone").value("0412345678"));
    }

    @Test
    void errorRejectsTooFewDigits() throws Exception {
        ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
        o.put("telephone", "12345");
        createOwner(o).andExpect(status().isBadRequest());
    }
}
```
The stated rule: on create, strip every non-digit from telephone, then require exactly 10 digits (else 400). `coreStripsToTenDigits` posts `(04) 1234-5678` and expects the stored/returned value `0412345678`. `errorRejectsTooFewDigits` posts `12345` and expects 400.

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`
Abstract base: `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles={OWNER_ADMIN,VET_ADMIN,ADMIN})`. Key helpers:
- `ownerNode()` — fully-valid unique owner JSON (firstName "Test", unique lastName/address/city, `uniqueTelephone()` = `04%08d`).
- `createOwner(body)` -> `POST /api/owners`; `createOwnerOk(body)` -> expects 2xx and returns id; `getOwner(id)` -> `GET /api/owners/{id}`; `extractId(...)` reads `id` from body or the `Location` header.
- `uniqueTelephone()` returns a 10-digit `04XXXXXXXX` number (comment notes the whole telephone rule chain: normalize-to-10, later E.164 +61 etc.).
Also `AuditLogCapture.java` in the same package (audit test support, not telephone-specific).

